4. **Checks (CI's order) in `.tools/wt-b613-fix` after the commit:** web: `npm run lint` (rc 0, `--max-warnings=0`), `npm run typecheck` (rc 0), `npm test` (whole suite; tests passed/failed/skipped = the step-1 counts plus exactly your added rows; names lost 0, added = yours, by `vitest --reporter=json` at base and head keyed by file and full name; control: one name dropped from a scratch copy reports lost 1). Repeat `customer-name.test.ts` and `e2e-runner.test.ts` 50 times in each pool: 0 red. **The vitest title hazard:** vitest cuts a `$what` interpolation longer than 40 characters in an `it.each` title, so two cells whose labels differ only after that point share a name (found by an earlier lane's run; the gate also found a pre-existing duplicate in another file); keep every new label short and distinct, and assert it by program for your own tables (the count of distinct titles equals the count of cells). Api: build both test projects with the project's warning settings (a warning that CI fails on is yours to fix), the two class filters green on SQLite, and the TRX case names of the two classes at base and head (names lost 0; names added = your new cases, 9 Api cells in Item 1 and 12 or more Feedback cells in Item 2), the whole Api test project and the whole Feedback project once if load allows (say so if you could not).
5. **Mutant battery** (the mutants named above) in `.tools/wt-b613-mut` (detached at the Stamp main sha), one mutant at a time, never committed; each restored by writing the original bytes back and proved (sha256 equal and `git diff --quiet` rc 0). For the Api and Feedback mutants build once per mutant (a build is slow: run the named mutants first, then the regression controls as time allows, and say what was cut). For the mock and the runner, run several mutants of one file in one vitest process where you can, and state how many ran. The mutant tree needs its own `npm ci` (heavy lock).
6. **Property check by program (print it).** (a) `git diff --name-only <main sha>..HEAD` = exactly the paths you changed among the 4 (control: a planted extra path is flagged). (b) every removed line of the four files printed and accounted (expected: in `e2e-runner.test.ts` the changed lines of Item 3 (the markerStep line, and the read lines of the rows you made comment-proof, each printed with its replacement); **0 removed lines in the other three files** unless a trailing comma forces one re-added pair, which you print; control: a planted removed line is counted). (c) **no product, tooling, workflow or support file:** `git diff --name-only <main sha>..HEAD | /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^(api/src/|api/tests/HpsmPoc\.Api\.Tests/Support/|api/tests/HpsmPoc\.Modules\.Feedback\.Tests/Support/|api/tests/HpsmPoc\.Api\.Tests/Hosting/|web/src/server/mock/customer-detail\.ts|web/scripts/|web/e2e/|web/src/audit-dev|web/src/e2e-runner\.liveApiRun|\.github/|web/package|web/vitest)'` = 0 (control: a scratch list holding `api/src/x.cs` reads 1). (d) **0 non-ASCII bytes added** in each file (`git diff | LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^\+.*[^ -~]'` = 0; control: a planted raw byte counts 1): hidden characters in the new rows are escapes only. (e) `git status --short` lists the paths you changed only. (f) gitleaks over the range and the commit message (`/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks`; a random `ghp_`-shaped canary fires rc 1, then the real scan rc 0, chained with `&&` in `bash -c`). (g) a test never sleeps to make a time-based assertion pass, never reads a person's name, and carries no `skip`, `todo`, `Skip =`, `.only`, `runIf`/`skipIf` or environment-gated early return that is new (grep your diff: 0 each; controls: a planted line of each is counted; the existing `TestDatabase.SqlServer` branch in `Hpsmpoc178CustomerNameTests.cs` is not yours and not in your diff). (h) no commit message or added line holds a person's name, a decision-card id or a ticket key (grep with a positive control). (i) **CodeQL pre-scan of your added lines (binding):** CodeQL's `js/file-system-race` (a check on a path, then a use of the same path: `existsSync`, `statSync` or `accessSync` followed by `readFileSync` or a write on it) flagged an earlier lane's test file (alert #13 on PR #211, fixed in code, never dismissed). Your Item 3 touches a file that already calls `existsSync` and `statSync` (for example `:675`, `:689`, `:769`, `:773`): add NO new check-then-use pair, and if a row you change holds one, say so in STATUS and leave it as it is. Grep your added lines for `existsSync|statSync|accessSync|lstatSync` and for any template that puts text from `process.env` or a file into a `console` / log call (js/log-injection): the count of added lines is printed, each is read, zero control: a planted line counts. (j) the real tracked files `web/scripts/e2e.mjs`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `Requests.cs`, `customer-detail.ts` and both helper copies have the same sha256 in all three worktrees after every full run.
